Station: Kenpoly-convocation-arena, Bori Metropolis.

The VES interpretation reveals a five-layer subsurface profile. The sequence begins with two resistive layers (1434 and 1879 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$), followed by a low-resistivity layer of 318 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$ at a depth of 2.5m to 25.9m. This is succeeded by a high-resistivity layer (3488 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$) and a final layer of 542 $\Omega\cdot\text{m}$. The resistivity transitions (K-H-K) characterize the profile. This calculated curve type is consistent with the KHK-type classification currently on file for this station.

